Subject: [PATCH 19/61] =?UTF-8?q?kt=5Fep=5Fwrapper:=20B2=20direct-UVA=20ex?=
 =?UTF-8?q?perts=20(KT=5FB2=5FUVA=5FEXPERTS)=20=E2=80=94=20pinned-host=20c?=
 =?UTF-8?q?opy=20of=20the=20last=20N=20CPU=20experts=20computed=20by=20Fla?=
 =?UTF-8?q?shInfer's=20SM120=20MXFP4=20MoE=20over=20UVA=20on=20a=20side=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?stream,=20gated=20to=20bs<=3DKT=5FB2=5FMAX=5FTOKENS=20(recipe?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20T3.18=20/=20E30)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each TP rank runs its slice of the N tail CPU experts straight out of pinned
host memory (device pointer of cudaHostAlloc'd weights; the grouped GEMM issues
the PCIe reads) so their bytes leave the CCD fabric for the two PCIe links.
kt-kernel sees them as -1 for those forwards but still loads all CPU experts,
so forwards above KT_B2_MAX_TOKENS (default 1) hand them back to kt: at |S|=40
a 13-token short prefill hit most of S per layer and put 10-13 ms of PCIe-bound
GEMM on the critical path (TTFT 0.61 -> 2.5 s). The B2 GEMM is forked onto a
per-device side stream after submit() and joined after sync(); FlashInfer's
cutlass_fused_moe allocates its workspace per call on the current stream and
only sets tactics host-side under a mutex, so it shares no device state with
the resident tier's call. submit() takes the kt expert count per call.

Measured (recipe evidence/t318-b2-prototype/): bit-equal to device weights,
graph replay works, ~0.21 ms per expert hit at 39-41 GiB/s vs ~0.146 ms for
kt's full-expert read; C1 41.92 -> 42.71 summed / 39.86 -> 40.71 wall at |S|=40,
40.65 / 38.73 at |S|=60; C4 unchanged. Verdict: experiment kept, default 0.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
