+# B2 direct-UVA experts (recipe T3.18, migration roadmap Stage 2 item 0): the
+# last KT_B2_UVA_EXPERTS CPU-resident experts of every MoE layer are *also*
+# kept in pinned host memory in the GPU kernel's layout, and on forwards of
+# at most KT_B2_MAX_TOKENS tokens each TP rank runs FlashInfer's SM120 MXFP4
+# MoE over its slice of them straight out of host memory (UVA device pointer,
+# PCIe reads issued by the GEMM itself) on a side stream, joined after
+# kt-kernel's sync. Their bytes leave the CPU-core/CCD path (E1b/E25 ceiling
+# ~125 GB/s) for the two PCIe links (E4b: additive, ~53 GiB/s each). kt-kernel
+# sees those experts as -1 (skipped) but still holds them, so larger forwards
+# hand them back to it. Streamed prefill chunks are unaffected (they already
+# run every CPU expert on the GPU). Requires KT_GPU_PREFILL_MIN_TOKENS > 0
+# (the export path is reused once at load time).
+# Verdict (recipe T3.18 / E30, 2026-09-24): kept as an experiment, NOT a
+# default. Bit-equal and graph-capturable, but one PCIe link per rank reads an
+# expert slice in ~0.21 ms vs ~0.146 ms for kt's full-expert read at 125 GB/s,
+# so B2 only adds bandwidth, never speed per expert: C1 41.9 -> 42.7 tok/s at
+# |S|=40 (+2 %), 40.7 at |S|=60 (B2 becomes the longest pole). 0 (default)
+# disables it.
+KT_B2_UVA_EXPERTS = int(os.environ.get("KT_B2_UVA_EXPERTS", "0"))
+# B2 runs only for forwards of at most this many MoE tokens; larger eager
+# forwards (short prefill below KT_GPU_PREFILL_MIN_TOKENS, big decode batches)
+# hand the B2 experts back to kt-kernel, which keeps a copy of them. At |S|=40
+# a 13-token prefill layer hit most of S and B2's ~0.21 ms/expert-hit put
+# 10-13 ms/step of PCIe-bound GEMM on the critical path (TTFT 0.61 -> 2.5 s,
+# T3.18 S=40 run); per-token B2 cost also exceeds kt's per-expert cost once
+# several tokens share the batch.
+KT_B2_MAX_TOKENS = int(os.environ.get("KT_B2_MAX_TOKENS", "1"))
 
 
